'' A user '&' chain over a wide-casting UDT mixed with narrow builtins lowers whole, and
'' the operator is mangled 'cat' as fbc spells it.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/udt-cat-operator-chain.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: _Zv23catR2DSR8FBSTRING
'' EXPECT-NOT: _Zv21&

'' ...AND THE CHAIN AROUND 'str( h )' IS WIDE, because the UDT's cast is. fbc emits no
'' conversion for it -- 'uint16* vr$15 = _ZN2DScvwEv( &H$0 ); fb_WstrConcatAW( "[", 2,
'' vr$15 )' -- and tiko-lang narrowed the lot, which a console hides and a REDIRECTED
'' run shows: goldenrun had fbc printing UTF-16 bytes here and tiko printing ASCII.
'' Both now write the same bytes.
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_WstrConcatAW
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_WstrConcatWA
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_PrintWstr
'' EXPECT-NOT: fb_PrintString
